{
  "about": "The fixed Ask set on the demo workspace (#513). Each question is asked in a zone's window, or in none. `find` is what the assistant's first step hands the retrieval for it: a route, the words to look for, and where. The run does not ask a model for it, so the same questions reach the same retrieval on every release. `expect` is what the retrieval must admit: `first` the record ranked first, `any` records that must be among those admitted, `none` records that must never be, `outcome` records, none (nothing found) or asks (the box asks which zone or which name, and reads nothing), `wall` whether the search reported a record held back by a wall (a window reads its own zone only, so the other side's records are never candidates: for those the check is `none`), `has` and `lacks` text the admitted records must hold or must not. Paths are matched as a part of the record's path. `cites` is what an answer must cite, checked with --model claude.",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "lately-acme",
      "kind": "lately",
      "window": "Work",
      "q": "What happened lately with Acme?",
      "find": {
        "route": "meetings",
        "words": [
          "acme"
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "outcome": "records",
        "first": "261105-acme-supplier-map-review",
        "none": [
          "Birch"
        ],
        "wall": false,
        "order": "recent"
      }
    },
